          "stage_one_comment": "TMCV is up about 14% since our June 7 Watchlist call, well ahead of the Nifty 50's roughly 2%. That is a real gap and worth flagging, but it has not been earned by resolution of either risk we said would move the rating: the Iveco Group deal is still not closed (France and Spain regulators have not signed off yet), and we could not confirm from public sources whether the TMF Holdings-related AGM vote on June 29 passed comfortably or with real institutional pushback -- coverage says a related-party resolution was approved, but not the margin. Nothing in the filings changed the ~80% downside case if Iveco closes fully debt-funded, and that risk is still live. We are treating this as the market getting ahead of an unresolved binary, not as confirmation we were wrong -- but the gap is now large enough that a materially lower entry point no longer exists if the binary resolves favorably, which cuts into the safety margin of waiting. We are not chasing the rally. Hold Watchlist; revisit hard at Q1 FY27 results and on any Iveco financing-structure disclosure."
